From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaradhana Sahu <aaradhana.sahu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:53:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: Make RXDMA buffer ring size configurable per
 memory profile

Currently, the RXDMA buffer ring size is hardcoded to 4096 and shared
across all memory profiles. This prevents individual profiles from tuning
the ring size based on their memory and performance requirements.

Add the RXDMA buffer ring size to the memory profile configuration and
implement ath12k_dp_rxdma_buf_ring_size() static inline function to
access the configured value. This allows different memory profiles to
select an appropriate ring size based on available system resources.

Tested-on: QCN9274 hw2.0 PCI WLAN.WBE.1.6-01243-QCAHKSWPL_SILICONZ-1
Tested-on: WCN7850 hw2.0 PCI WLAN.HMT.1.1.c7-00108-QCAHMTSWPL_V1.0_V2.0_SILICONZ_UPSTREAM-3
Tested-on: QCC2072 hw1.0 PCI WLAN.COL.1.0.c2-00074-QCACOLSWPL_V1_TO_SILICONZ-1

Signed-off-by: Aaradhana Sahu <aaradhana.sahu@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Baochen Qiang <baochen.qiang@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Rameshkumar Sundaram <rameshkumar.sundaram@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261007-mpp_ws-v1-1-739b1fb87d24@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Jeff Johnson <jeff.johnson@oss.qualcomm.com>

[ upstream commit 643f0bf93617 in linux-next (ath-next, ath12k), not in v7.3-rc7 ]
[ ported: v7.3-rc7 keeps the per-profile DP sizes in core.h and reads
  them through the DP_*_SIZE(ab) macros of dp.h, so the size becomes
  DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE(ab) instead of a static inline accessor; same
  values (4096 in both profiles) ]
[ upstream author: Aaradhana Sahu <aaradhana.sahu@oss.qualcomm.com>; picked for the iceland kernel q89s ]
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c  | 2 ++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h  | 1 +
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.h    | 3 ++-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c | 2 +-
 4 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
index bf20e842276e..482b65844343 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -59,6 +59,7 @@ ath12k_mem_profile_based_param ath12k_mem_profile_based_param[] = {
 			.num_pool_tx_desc = 32768,
 			.rx_desc_count = 12288,
 			.rx_release_ring_size = 16384,
+			.rxdma_buf_ring_size = 4096,
 		},
 	},
 [ATH12K_QMI_MEMORY_MODE_LOW_512_M] = {
@@ -73,6 +74,7 @@ ath12k_mem_profile_based_param ath12k_mem_profile_based_param[] = {
 			.num_pool_tx_desc = 16384,
 			.rx_desc_count = 6144,
 			.rx_release_ring_size = 8192,
+			.rxdma_buf_ring_size = 4096,
 		},
 	},
 };
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
index a326f1553359..d154548ba93a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.h
@@ -935,6 +935,7 @@ struct ath12k_dp_profile_params {
 	u32 num_pool_tx_desc;
 	u32 rx_desc_count;
 	u32 rx_release_ring_size;
+	u32 rxdma_buf_ring_size;
 };
 
 struct ath12k_mem_profile_based_param {
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.h
index dc800134536f..cd4220cc55a9 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.h
@@ -205,7 +205,8 @@ struct ath12k_pdev_dp {
 #define DP_REO_EXCEPTION_RING_SIZE	128
 #define DP_REO_CMD_RING_SIZE		256
 #define DP_REO_STATUS_RING_SIZE		2048
-#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE		4096
+#define DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE(ab) \
+	((ab)->profile_param->dp_params.rxdma_buf_ring_size)
 #define DP_RX_MAC_BUF_RING_SIZE		4096
 #define DP_RXDMA_REFILL_RING_SIZE	2048
 #define DP_RXDMA_ERR_DST_RING_SIZE	1024
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
index f220c950d6a2..2f49aa5f12e9 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
@@ -1803,7 +1803,7 @@ int ath12k_dp_rx_alloc(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	ret = ath12k_dp_srng_setup(ab,
 				   &dp->rx_refill_buf_ring.refill_buf_ring,
 				   HAL_RXDMA_BUF, 0, 0,
-				   DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE);
+				   DP_RXDMA_BUF_RING_SIZE(ab));
 	if (ret) {
 		ath12k_warn(ab, "failed to setup rx_refill_buf_ring\n");
 		return ret;
-- 
2.43.0

